{
  "slug": "tinman-heartbeat-for-claude-code",
  "name": "Tinman Heartbeat For Claude Code",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Adds scheduled health monitoring to Claude Code. Define a HEARTBEAT.md checklist for your project and TinMan runs it through Claude on demand or on a timer. Claude analyzes your codebase against the checklist (uncommitted changes, failing tests, stale branches, disk space, whatever you care about) and reports what needs attention. Results are logged and can forward to Telegram via C3Poh. Three security presets control autonomy: sane (notify only, default), paranoid (read-only), and chaos (Claude can act). Zero external dependencies beyond Python 3.9+ and Claude CLI.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 commands**, `tinman-heartbeat`, `tinman-status`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install tinman-heartbeat-for-claude-code@claude-community` from `andyuninvited/tinman_for_claudecode`.\n\nTinMan adds a proactive heartbeat to your Claude Code setup. Instead of waiting for you to ask, Claude runs a scheduled health check and tells you when something needs attention — disk space, uncommitted code, stale branches, failed tool calls, whatever you care about.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
